<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badra, Iraq</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badra is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wasit">Wasit</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, close to the Iranian border at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains. Near it lies Tell Aqar, the site of the ancient city of Der, which guarded the route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>. The town is surrounded by date palm groves and lies on an old trade and pilgrim route between Iraq and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/badra-iraq.jpg" alt="Badra, Iraq" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alrafidain TV · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badra,_Wasit_-_Jul_3,_2018.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
